{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>You shall prepare it upon the burnt offering.</b> Together with the burnt offering. A precedent: 'it shall be reckoned to the field of the land.' Why is 'upon the burnt offering or for a sacrifice' stated? Since it is stated above, 'you shall make a fire-offering, a burnt offering or a sacrifice' — I might hear that if one said 'upon me is a burnt offering,' 'upon me is a meal offering,' 'upon me is a peace offering,' he brings one libation for two. Scripture says, <b>upon the burnt offering or for a sacrifice</b> — this tells that he brings for this one by itself and for that one by itself."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:03.186525144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}